# EI-CF without ROBOT

This directory contains the EI-CF active-search baseline used to isolate the
effect of ROBOT. It uses the same Gaussian-process output models and composite
detectability function as EI-CF+ROBOT, but applies no trust-region or diversity
filter.

For each candidate input, EI-CF draws posterior samples of the predicted
outputs and evaluates the composite detection score. With `--active-search`,
the acquisition is the mean predicted detectability rather than improvement
over the current best value. The highest-scoring candidate is sent to NMMA,
and one new event is produced per iteration.

## Environment

```bash
export NMMA_WORKDIR=/path/to/nmma/source/checkout
export SVD_PATH=/path/to/svdmodels
export PRIOR_FILE=/path/to/priors/Bu2019lm.prior
export OUTPUT_BASE="$PWD/out"
```

## Paper configuration

Single seed:

```bash
python -u run_bo.py \
  --seed 1 \
  --n-iterations 80 \
  --output-folder out/eicf_no_robot/seed_1 \
  --acquisition EI \
  --active-search \
  --candidate-samples 1500 \
  --eicf-mc-samples 16 \
  --no-plots
```

Three seeds:

```bash
python -u run_multi_seed.py \
  --seeds 1-3 \
  --n-iterations 80 \
  --output-root out/eicf_no_robot \
  --candidate-samples 1500 \
  --eicf-mc-samples 16 \
  --no-plots
```

The run records `algorithm_overhead_seconds` for each event, allowing overhead
to be averaged over the same first-80-event budget used for the paper table.
The bundled metric scripts calculate measurable fraction and the summed
eight-dimensional marginal KL using fixed bins derived from the initial
measurable training events.
